# The chip's engines (gold.il) against the ungated ones the proofs read, each start taken
# only once certified (gate.il), flops cut open (side.ys). miter -equiv wants the same ports,
# so every flop has a namesake. From the same flops and inputs both drive the same outputs
# and next flops, so from any one state they agree for all time on all but refused.
# Trusted: yosys's frontend, proc, flatten, memory_map, dffunmap, expose, miter and sat.
read_rtlil gold.il
read_rtlil gate.il
miter -equiv -flatten gold gate miter
hierarchy -top miter
sat -verify -prove trigger 0
